=========================================================================
SIMPLE EXAMPLE: Automic watches the folder, Automic logs + moves the file
=========================================================================
No Oracle-side scheduling needed here -- Automic does the watching, and
just calls plain SQL. This is the simplest of the options we've covered.

Two Automic objects, one Oracle table.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 -- Oracle table (run once)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

CREATE TABLE file_watcher_log (
    id              NUMBER GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    file_name       VARCHAR2(500)  NOT NULL,
    file_path       VARCHAR2(4000) NOT NULL,
    dest_path       VARCHAR2(4000),
    detected_at     TIMESTAMP DEFAULT SYSTIMESTAMP
);


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2 -- FA object (File Event) in Automic
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Object name : FA.INBOUND.DROP
Agent       : the agent that can see /data/inbound
Path        : /data/inbound
Filename    : *.*
Check       : enable "check file size" (e.g. 2 checks, 15s apart) so it
              doesn't fire on a file that's still being written
Action      : Start Task -> JOBS.LOG_AND_MOVE_FILE  (Step 3)

Activate the FA object once configured.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3 -- JOBS object (SQL) in Automic
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Object name : JOBS.LOG_AND_MOVE_FILE
Login object: your Oracle DB login object
Script tab:

    INSERT INTO file_watcher_log (file_name, file_path, dest_path)
    VALUES (
        '&$AE_FILE_NAME#',
        '&$AE_PATH_NAME#/&$AE_FILE_NAME#',
        '/data/processed/&$AE_FILE_NAME#'
    );
    COMMIT;

Post-process tab (moves the physical file after the insert succeeds --
run as an OS script step on the same agent as the FA object):

    mv "&$AE_PATH_NAME#/&$AE_FILE_NAME#" "/data/processed/&$AE_FILE_NAME#"

(&$AE_FILE_NAME# and &$AE_PATH_NAME# are populated automatically by
Automic from the triggering FA object. If your Automic version names
these variables differently, check Process Monitoring > Variables on a
completed run of JOBS.LOG_AND_MOVE_FILE to confirm the exact names.)


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
THAT'S IT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Drop a file in /data/inbound ->
  FA.INBOUND.DROP detects it ->
  JOBS.LOG_AND_MOVE_FILE inserts a row, then moves the file.

Check it worked:
    SELECT * FROM file_watcher_log ORDER BY detected_at DESC;

If you later want more (checksum, error handling, dedup on re-drops,
retry logic), the earlier oracle_native_filewatcher.sql and
automic_filewatcher_setup.txt files have the fuller version -- this one
is intentionally stripped down to just "detect, log, move."
